# p5 usage: /usage after two billed turns (billed-turns.json: cacheRead 4000
# and 30000, reasoning 900), the footer's context and session segments on,
# under the pinned clock (2026-10-12 15:30 UTC) and with no usage cache. The
# first open's read is a path the fake does not know (`usage off`): 404, so
# fx v0.0.16 shows its message-only failure, and the keys on it (no Esc until
# the end: on that screen Esc closes it). Then r with the report answered
# (p5-usage-report-turns.json, each read held 1.5 s): fetching..., then today,
# the six finished days and the month to yesterday (policy.zig:57-89@481104fd),
# the two turns as the report counts them. Then /cost, /usage with an argument,
# /stats and /credits. Old fx counts the turns locally. `home` keeps what each
# binary persisted; `gwlog` what was asked.
clock 1791819000000
usage off
models models.json
gateway billed-turns.json
wait 2.5
type /statusline context
key Enter
wait 1
type /statusline session
key Enter
wait 1
snap launch
type first question
key Enter
wait 5
type second question
key Enter
wait 5
snap turns
type /usage
wait 0.7
snap typed
key Enter
wait 3
snap open
key Down
wait 0.5
snap down
key Enter
wait 0.7
snap enter
key Tab
wait 1
snap tab
key BTab
wait 1
snap btab
key Right
wait 1
snap right
key Left
wait 1
snap left
usage p5-usage-report-turns.json
key r
wait 1
snap fetching
wait 8
snap r
key Tab
wait 0.7
snap r-today
key Tab
wait 0.7
snap r-7d
key Escape
wait 0.5
snap esc
type /cost
wait 0.7
snap cost-typed
key Enter
wait 2
snap cost
type /usage 7d
key Enter
wait 2
snap arg
key Escape
wait 0.3
type /stats
key Enter
wait 1
snap stats
type /credits
key Enter
wait 2
snap credits
home end
gwlog
